    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0499" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4299: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-19T17:00:00+08:00">February 19, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 19—9:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. It is becoming increasingly apparent that Chinese troops will not withdraw.
                    Hostilities on a larger scale than heretofore are possible within next day or
                    two in which case shells may land in Settlement, particularly in Yangtzepoo and
                    Hongkew areas. I have advised Americans in those areas to take cover as far away
                    as possible while firing is in progress and to seek places of greater safety and
                    have urged that women and children be transferred to places of greater safety
                    either this afternoon or tomorrow morning. News items in the <pb facs="0500"
                        n="396" xml:id="pg396"/> foregoing sense will be published in afternoon
                    papers February 19th and morning papers of 20th.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d417-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation, Nanking and Tokyo for information.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d417-f1" n="71" xml:id="d417-f1-content">
                <p>The Department replied in telegram No. 44, February 20, 1 p.m., that it “approves
                    action taken.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
